Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.50,0:00:03.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}This is a reproducibility study of Graph Edit Networks,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.01,0:00:11.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}a graph neural network output layer that predicts how a graph changes over time as a sequence of interpretable edits.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.49,0:00:17.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The reproduction re-implements the model and re-tests the paper's four experimental claims.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.60,0:00:21.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Graph time-series prediction asks a model to forecast the next graph in a sequence,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.73,0:00:25.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}not just a label.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.87,0:00:29.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Standard graph networks emit node or edge probabilities,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.00,0:00:34.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}which can't naturally express the structural operations that transform one graph into the next.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.44,0:00:38.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Graph Edit Networks close this gap by predicting an explicit,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.51,0:00:40.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}human-readable edit script.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.31,0:00:45.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The original work claims it beats every baseline, reaches perfect accuracy on trees,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.92,0:00:51.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and scales to large graphs, but those claims rest on briefly-described benchmarks,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.39,0:00:54.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}where independent reproduction adds value.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.49,0:01:00.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The reproduction contributes four things: it re-runs the model and baseline to check each claim;
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.42,0:01:04.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}it documents the synthetic data generators the paper omitted;
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.19,0:01:07.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}it adds a cleaner setup separating training and test series;
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.89,0:01:12.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and it shows some benchmarks let the model win by memorising seen transitions.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.01,0:01:19.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}A graph edit network attaches to a standard GNN backbone and predicts a script of edits: insert,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:19.54,0:01:23.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}delete or replace a node, or insert or delete an edge.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.21,0:01:27.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Applying them in sequence maps the current graph to the next.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.35,0:01:32.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Training uses reference mappings from graph-edit-distance approximators,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.25,0:01:35.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}with two loss variants, hinge and cross-entropy,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.51,0:01:38.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and edge-filtering for citation graphs.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:38.46,0:01:43.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Benchmarks span three families: dynamical graph systems like Edit Cycles,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:43.24,0:01:45.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Degree Rules and Game of Life;
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.20,0:01:50.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}tree systems for Boolean-formula simplification and Peano addition; and, for scaling,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.77,0:01:56.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}an arXiv citation network of about twenty-seven thousand papers yielding fifteen hundred
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.53,0:01:59.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}sub-graphs up to nearly three thousand nodes.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.78,0:02:07.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Three of the four original claims hold: the model beats the variational-autoencoder baseline on every dynamical task,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.40,0:02:12.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}reaches near-perfect accuracy on trees, and its forward pass grows sub-quadratically.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:12.94,0:02:17.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The fourth fails: backward passes were claimed to scale linearly,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.18,0:02:20.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}but the fitted exponent is clearly above one.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.41,0:02:26.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Two robustness checks: swapping the ad-hoc initialisation for Erdős–Rényi and configuration-model
Dialogue: 0,0:02:26.80,0:02:29.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}generators barely changes any metric,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:29.23,0:02:33.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and adding a proper held-out test set lowers scores slightly.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.25,0:02:38.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}But a deeper diagnostic finds the tree generators mostly produce unsimplifiable trees,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.91,0:02:44.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}only thirteen percent of Boolean and twenty-six percent of Peano samples are usable,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.44,0:02:46.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}undercutting those tasks.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.39,0:02:50.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The verdict is nuanced: Graph Edit Networks are reproducible,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:50.55,0:02:53.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}elegant and interpretable, and most claims hold.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.82,0:02:58.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}But one scaling claim is wrong, backward passes are super-linear,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.24,0:03:04.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and several benchmarks reward memorising seen transitions rather than genuine generalisation.
